00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.210
The second thing that
I wanted to mention we

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.910
talked about in the
submission space,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:46.340
it's really critical that
you have a package management

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.450
solution.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.530
And so RStudio offers RStudio
package manager as one option

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.100
there.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:57.230
And we're excited to announce
Bioconductor as a new addition

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.820
to that offering.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:03.320
And so just kind of quickly
show you what that looks like.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:06.410
If you're using packages
from Bioconductor,

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.270
you might be familiar
with this notion

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:12.800
that Bioconductor does its
releases about twice a year.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.790
And so package manager
makes those same releases

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.030
available to you.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.530
There's instructions for
inside of package manager

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.390
for how to set up.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:25.490
One of the things we're
really excited about

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:26.930
is that previously,
